# Everything here is excluded from the build context sent to the Docker daemon.
# Without this file the context is ~119 MB, almost all of it web/node_modules —
# re-uploaded on every build, for files the backend image never uses.

# Frontend: not part of the backend image at all.
web/

# VCS and local tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Secrets and local config. The image must get these from env at runtime, never
# baked in at build time — a committed layer keeps them forever.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build outputs and caches
bin/
dist/
coverage/
*.out
*.test

# Editor / OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Docs are not needed to compile. agent_documentation/ holds design write-ups,
# docs/ is the generated Swagger package and IS needed (it is a Go package
# imported by main), so it is deliberately not excluded here.
agent_documentation/
README.md
